"1959","On the authority of Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him): A man from the Ansar had two stallions that became unruly/mature. He put them in a walled garden and locked the door on them. Then he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanting him to supplicate for him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting with a group of the Ansar. The man said: ""O Prophet of Allah, I have come for a need, and I have two stallions that became unruly, so I put them in a walled garden and locked the door on them, and I would like you to supplicate for me that Allah may subdue them for me."" He said to his companions: ""Stand up with us."" So he went until he reached the door and said: ""Open it."" The door was opened, and one of the two stallions was near the door. When it saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), it prostrated to him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Bring me something to tie its head with, and give me control over it."" He brought a rope/halter, so he tied its head and gained control over it. Then they walked to the far end of the garden to the other stallion. When it saw him, it fell down prostrating. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the man: ""Bring me something to tie its head with."" So he tied its head and gained control over it, and said: ""Go, for they will not disobey you."" When the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw that, they said: ""O Messenger of Allah, these are two stallions that do not reason, yet they prostrated to you. Should we not prostrate to you?"" He said: ""I do not command anyone to prostrate to anyone. And if I were to command anyone to prostrate to anyone, I would have commanded the woman to prostrate to her husband."""
